# ====================================================
# HELIX — Environment Variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in your values
# ====================================================

# Supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# App
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Auto-login — REMOVED. Do not reintroduce these keys.
#
# The auth screen used to be one button whose credentials came from
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_EMAIL / NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_PASSWORD (and a BYPASS_* legacy pair).
# A `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable is inlined into the client bundle by Next, so that
# shipped a live account password to every visitor who opened devtools. Wave 0
# replaced the button with a real email-and-password form; nothing in `src/`
# reads any of the six names any more, and `src/tests/api-auth.test.ts` plus
# `e2e/smoke.test.ts` assert against the SERVED bundle so it cannot come back.
#
# Still outstanding by hand, and this file is what will undo them if it keeps
# saying otherwise: delete NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_* and NEXT_PUBLIC_BYPASS_* from the
# Netlify environment, then rotate that Supabase account's password — it was
# public in the bundle and has not been changed since.
